  "method": "Analytic planar opacity-kernel model and CPU float64 midpoint quadrature only. All depths are measured from the OLD outer field coordinate F=.025km (d=F-.025km), including the empty lead of the sharp profile. F is treated as an affine physical distance with unit gradient solely in this model. rho=M*clamp(U), sigma=beta*rho, T=exp(-tau), kernel=sigma*T. Integration uses exact piecewise tau evaluated at segment midpoints with0.25/0.5m steps until endpoint T<1e-6. Numeric moments are normalized by integrated midpoint mass. Analytic full moments and separately conditioned cutoff moments distinguish quadrature error from discarded tail. tau1 numeric uses linear interpolation of exact endpoint depths. No volume generation, half quantization, trilinear/voxel reconstruction, camera, scene source variation, GPU/rendering, tone mapping or pixel-sharpness prediction.",
